    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah after wind, hail, or storm damage, follow these structured steps:"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Document the Damage Safely"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take clear photos and videos of the damage from the ground or using a safe vantage point.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Note the exact date and time the storm or weather event occurred.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cover active, urgent leaks temporarily with a tarp only if it is safe to do so. Do not make permanent repairs before your insurer inspects the property.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Get a Professional Roof Inspection"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contact a local, licensed Utah roofing contractor (such as local specialists found via Yelp Provo Roofing & Claim Services or companies like USA Superior Storm Damage Guide ) to perform a comprehensive roof evaluation.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Yelp Provo Roofing & Claim Services",
                "link": "https://www.yelp.com/questions/loc/provo-ut/hail-storm-roof-looks-beat-im-filing-insurance-claim-want/fORQHQvz8Hy1vruVeDCnYw"
              },
              {
                "text": "USA Superior Storm Damage Guide",
                "link": "https://usasuperior.com/storm-damage-roof/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ensure they document the surface, flashing, underlayment, and decking\u2014not just missing shingles\u2014to help prevent overlooked claim details.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ask if the roofer is willing to meet your insurance adjuster on-site during their inspection.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Review Your Insurance Policy"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check your policy for your specific wind and hail deductible (which may be a flat dollar amount or a percentage of your home's insured value)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Confirm your coverage type (Replacement Cost Value vs. Actual Cash Value)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. File the Claim with Your Insurer"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contact your homeowner's insurance company as soon as possible (most insurers have a filing window of 6 to 24 months from the date of the storm, though acting quickly is always better).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Provide the date of loss, a brief description of the damage, and any initial photo documentation.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Meet the Adjuster and Review the Estimate"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "An insurance adjuster will schedule a visit (typically within 3 to 14 days) to inspect the roof. Have your contractor's report and estimate ready to share on-site."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Wait for the initial insurance scope and first payment/settlement offer (usually 7 to 21 days after the adjuster's visit) . If the insurance estimate misses hidden damage or flashing repairs, your roofer can submit a supplement request.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help you narrow this down, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What kind of damage happened (hail, high winds, fallen tree, leak)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How long ago did the storm occur?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
